# Month 1 Summary — GeoDev Lab Africa

## Project Title

### Healthcare Accessibility Analysis in Villupuram District, Tamil Nadu

**Project Question:**

> Which settlements in Villupuram district, Tamil Nadu, are more than 5 km by road from the nearest public health facility?

---

## 1. Project Overview

This project was developed throughout Month 1 of the GeoDev Lab Africa programme.

The aim is to investigate healthcare accessibility in Villupuram district, Tamil Nadu, by combining settlement locations, public health facilities, road-network data, and population information.

The project started with a clearly defined spatial question and progressed through data collection, data documentation, coordinate-system preparation, quality assessment, and vector analysis in QGIS/Python.

The Month 1 workflow demonstrates how a GIS question can be developed into a structured, analysis-ready project.

---

# Week 1 — Defining the Question

## Question

> Which settlements in Villupuram district, Tamil Nadu, are more than 5 km by road from the nearest public health facility?

## Why this question matters

Access to healthcare can vary between settlements depending on their location, available health facilities, and road connectivity.

Identifying settlements that are more than 5 km by road from the nearest public health facility can help highlight locations that may require further investigation of healthcare accessibility and transportation connectivity.

## Data identified

The project requires:

1. Villupuram district boundary
2. Settlement locations
3. Public health facilities
4. Road network
5. Population data

## Main data sources

- Tamil Nadu GIS (TNGIS) — district boundary
- OpenStreetMap — settlements, health facilities and road information
- Census of India 2011 — population information

