# Week 4 — Vector Analysis

Week 4 introduced vector analysis operations including:

- Buffer
- Dissolve/Union
- Intersection
- Spatial Join
- Layer styling
- Spreadsheet/table integration

The analysis was continued using the Villupuram healthcare-accessibility project.

## 5 km Health Facility Buffer

A 5 km buffer was created around the mapped health facilities.

The buffer was performed using the projected **EPSG:32644** dataset so that the distance was measured in metres.

The 5 km buffer represents **straight-line spatial coverage**.

It does not represent road-network travel distance.

## Union

The individual health-facility buffers were combined into a unified coverage area.

## Intersection

The coverage area was intersected with the Villupuram study boundary to keep the analysis within the project area.

## Spatial Join

The settlement layer was spatially joined with the 5 km health-facility coverage area.

This allowed settlements to be classified according to whether they fall inside or outside the 5 km straight-line coverage area.

