# Month 1 Learning

Through this project, I worked through the complete initial GIS workflow:

1. Define a spatial question.
2. Identify the data required.
3. Obtain real spatial data.
4. Document data sources and characteristics.
5. Inspect coordinate reference systems.
6. Reproject data into an appropriate projected CRS.
7. Clip data to the study area.
8. Check data quality.
9. Create buffers.
10. Perform union and intersection.
11. Perform spatial joins.
12. Produce an analysis map.
13. Organise the project into a reproducible GitHub repository.

The project also reinforced the relationship between GIS software workflows and future Python-based geospatial automation.

